{
  "source": "video-audit/vector-space-repair-2026-09-10/edited.wav",
  "duration": 209.2666875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.8,
      "text": "When AI processes language, it translates your words into rows of numbers called embeddings."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.28,
      "end": 11.1,
      "text": "But as the AI's internal layers process your message, they rewrite these numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.68,
      "end": 13.72,
      "text": "The values shift and update constantly."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.58,
      "end": 18.48,
      "text": "If the numbers don't stay the same, how can they reliably represent meaning?"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.2,
      "end": 24.42,
      "text": "To answer that, we have to look at how AI uses a mathematical concept called vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.12,
      "end": 31.58,
      "text": "This map shows three cities, each with a position defined by two dimensions, latitude and longitude."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.38,
      "end": 35.56,
      "text": "Dallas is at 33 degrees north, 97 degrees west."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.52,
      "end": 38.82,
      "text": "Mountain View and New York City have their own coordinates."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.5,
      "end": 41.94,
      "text": "These numbers give every city a fixed position."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.06,
      "end": 47.26,
      "text": "Now, let's say we introduce two completely new sets of coordinates to this map."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.8,
      "end": 53.18,
      "text": "One is at 38 north, 120 west, and the other is at 40 north, 76 west."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.18,
      "end": 57.26,
      "text": "Neither lands perfectly on our three cities. We measure the distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.98,
      "end": 65.96,
      "text": "When a position doesn't perfectly match a known entity, comparing the coordinates to find the smallest physical gap tells you the closest logical match."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.12,
      "end": 69.48,
      "text": "Let's apply that same logic to something conceptual."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.16,
      "end": 75.64,
      "text": "Here's a chart scoring three drinks, Coke, Pepsi, and coffee, across seven taste characteristics."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.52,
      "end": 82.32,
      "text": "Each drink gets a row of seven numbers, called a vector, plotting a precise position in seven-dimensional space."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.32,
      "end": 88.9,
      "text": "Coke and Pepsi have identical numbers for sweetness, fizz, and darkness, while coffee's numbers differ completely."
    },
    {
      "start": 89.54,
      "end": 97.98,
      "text": "Just as latitude and longitude anchor a physical city on a geographic map, these seven numerical ratings anchor a conceptual profile into vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.54,
      "end": 102.78,
      "text": "We can picture how these numerical vectors relate by plotting them on a map of similarities."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.56,
      "end": 110.24,
      "text": "Because Coke and Pepsi share nearly identical data rows, their positions sit right next to each other, forming a soft drinks neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.24,
      "end": 116.16,
      "text": "Coffee has a differing vector, so it sits far away, isolated in a hot drinks cluster."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.28,
      "end": 122.58,
      "text": "Here is a chart showing a mystery drink with a seven-dimension vector that doesn't exactly match the others."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.36,
      "end": 128.7,
      "text": "Look at the numbers. Nine, one, ten, two, three, eight, nine."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.56,
      "end": 131.38,
      "text": "Which known drink is the closest match?"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.14,
      "end": 134.4,
      "text": "The first six numbers match Pepsi exactly."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.4,
      "end": 139.84,
      "text": "The only difference is the citrus column, where the mystery drink scores a nine and Pepsi a ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.52,
      "end": 144.26,
      "text": "That's a gap of just one point, while the gap with Coke is eight points."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.04,
      "end": 147.06,
      "text": "This shows how conceptual distance works."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.84,
      "end": 151.0,
      "text": "We calculate the size of the numerical gaps in matching positions."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.92,
      "end": 155.04,
      "text": "Smaller gaps mean the concepts sit closer together in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.3,
      "end": 159.14,
      "text": "AI systems use this exact same mathematical structure."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.14,
      "end": 165.22,
      "text": "But instead of seven dimensions for taste, they use thousands of dimensions to plot the nuances of word meaning."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.06,
      "end": 169.68,
      "text": "Let's see this in action using the sentence mapped out here."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.26,
      "end": 174.66,
      "text": "The cat sat on the mat during the May rainstorm because it was tired."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.34,
      "end": 177.78,
      "text": "We will focus entirely on the word it."
    },
    {
      "start": 178.58,
      "end": 182.12,
      "text": "Initially, it begins with a set of generic baseline numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.6,
      "end": 186.32,
      "text": "But as the AI's internal layers process the surrounding context,"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.32,
      "end": 190.54,
      "text": "they rewrite those numbers to reflect its connection to the subject of the sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.3,
      "end": 196.78,
      "text": "By rewriting the values, the AI moves it across the thousands of dimensions in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 197.0,
      "end": 200.0,
      "text": "Its new position reflects its connection to cat in this sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 201.46,
      "end": 203.38,
      "text": "Meaning is a position in vector space."
    },
    {
      "start": 204.32,
      "end": 205.86,
      "text": "Similar meanings usually sit close together."
    }
  ],
